From: Retro Receipts replay lane
Subject: [PATCH] agent 0.3.24 — capture what re-simulation needs

Adds the AUTHORITATIVE input words + seat map + a character-select anchor snapshot, so a server can
re-simulate a match exactly instead of the tape trying to describe it.

Measured live on the Steam build (docs/STEAM-GGPO-DETERMINISM.md):
  * MvC2 ships verbatim GGPO rollback. It registers ONE region, blk[0..0x33B18) — that IS the
    complete deterministic simulation state (verified: size field at 0x140AC6EF8 reads 0x33B18).
  * The agent ALREADY reads that exact block every frame, so the anchor costs no extra read.
  * Input chain: G+0x218 (RAW) -> bit table @0x140A4F780 -> blk+0x3C66+i*0x14 -> cl+0x4fc.
    We ship cl+0x4fc today: TWO STAGES DOWNSTREAM and lossy.
  * KCODE_OFF is mislabelled "flycast kcode[0] (the LOCAL pad)". It is G+0x218 = GGPO SEAT 0's
    input. Which seat is local comes from G+0x258, which we never read — the root cause of the
    documented side-swap.
  * A CHARACTER-SELECT snapshot is portable across processes (proven: restored into another process
    with blk moved 36 MB, 804+243 pointers relocated, game continued at 60fps). A BATTLE snapshot is
    NOT — it holds 557 pointers into the per-character asset image and killed the game twice.

Columns are APPENDED, so positional consumers of existing columns are unaffected.

Apply from the repo root:
    git apply docs/patches/agent-0.3.24-replay-capture.patch

--- a/agent/src/reader.rs
+++ b/agent/src/reader.rs
@@
 const MATCH_ARR_ADD:   usize = 0x3f24;      // fighter_array = *(exe+MATCH_PTR_OFF) + this. ⚠ pointer chain — do NOT change
-const KCODE_OFF:       usize = 0xac6f58;    // flycast kcode[0] (the LOCAL pad) offset from the exe base
+// ⚠ CORRECTION (measured live 2026-08-26): this is NOT "flycast kcode[0] (the LOCAL pad)". It is
+// G+0x218 — GGPO SEAT 0's post-synchronisation input word. Which seat is LOCAL comes from
+// SEATMAP_OFF, which we never read; that omission is the root cause of the documented side-swap.
+const KCODE_OFF:       usize = 0xac6f58;    // = SEATIN_OFF (kept: existing references)
+const SEATIN_OFF:      usize = 0xac6f58;    // G+0x218: RAW input word, seat k at +k*4 (u32, 24-bit)
+const SEATMAP_OFF:     usize = 0xac6f98;    // G+0x258: GGPO player k -> seat index (i32, -1 unmapped)
+const ROLLBACK_OFF:    usize = 0xac74ac;    // G+0x76C: load_game_state count; >0 = GGPO rewound
+const ARENA_PTR_OFF:   usize = 0xac6d40;    // exe global -> the single 256 MiB arena blk is carved from
+const MODE_OFF:        usize = 0x3cb8;      // blk+0x3CB8: byte[2] 1 = CHARACTER SELECT, 2 = IN BATTLE
 const LOCALPLAYER_OFF: usize = 0xac7230;    // localPlayerNum: 0 = P1, 1 = P2 (flycast's own side global, next to kcode;
@@
-const GS_SCHEMA: &str = "[frame,p1_in,p2_in,kcode,hp[6],px[6],py[6],p1_meter,p2_meter,meter_fill,combo_dealt[6],combo_recv[6],vx[6],vy[6],red_hp[6],facing[6],hitstun[6],drawn[6],sid[6],atimer[6],eyeX,eyeY,ground]";
+// 0.3.24 appends seat_in[2]: the AUTHORITATIVE raw pad words (G+0x218+seat*4), upstream of the
+// 12-entry translation table. p1_in/p2_in are the downstream decoded values and are kept only for
+// compatibility — a re-simulator must use seat_in.
+const GS_SCHEMA: &str = "[frame,p1_in,p2_in,kcode,hp[6],px[6],py[6],p1_meter,p2_meter,meter_fill,combo_dealt[6],combo_recv[6],vx[6],vy[6],red_hp[6],facing[6],hitstun[6],drawn[6],sid[6],atimer[6],eyeX,eyeY,ground,seat_in[2]]";
@@
